-- NutriMarket presentation data. Runs after schema.sql on every startup (spring.sql.init.data-locations).
-- Every statement is idempotent: existing rows are kept, so rehearsal changes survive restarts.
-- To restore this exact baseline and prepare the demo scenarios, run DemoSeeder (see docs/DEMO_SCENARIOS.md).
--
-- Accounts (password: nutrimarket-demo): demo_ready, demo_live, demo_review, demo_expert, demo_new, demo_allergy,
--   demo_substitute, demo_replan and demo_shopper1..5.
--   demo_expert must be listed in nutrimarket.health.expert-usernames; experts cannot review their own data.
-- demo_ready and demo_live: health profile v1 (Australia/Sydney, type 2 diabetes, 1800-2200 kcal) and validated
--   meals for 2026-10-05..2026-10-11, already delivered to Agent 2. Meals carry a "NutriMarket demo seed"
--   provenance (no photo analysis); nutrition comes from pinned USDA entries.
-- demo_ready: 21 meals and the completed assessment for that week, cleared by demo_expert (cd8d7b6e-bebb-4cd3-899d-19066842ebc1).
-- demo_live: the same 21 meals as demo_ready, no assessment in a new database.
-- demo_review: copies of demo_live's meals without the Sunday 2026-10-11 dinner (the missing-meal prompt) and with
--   6-8 October reduced to small meals under 900 kcal a day, so its assessment needs expert review. Standing consent
--   to automatic planning is on.
-- demo_new: account only, so the first-login questionnaire opens.
-- demo_allergy, demo_substitute, demo_replan and demo_shopper1..5: accounts only; DemoSeeder adds their profiles,
--   meals, assessments, plans, matches, baskets and (shoppers) orders from demo-scenarios.json.
-- Meal plans are week-specific and expire, so they are not stored here.
SET time_zone = '+00:00';


